From: Frédéric Devernay <devernay@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] QMutex: fix a lost wake-up in the non-futex implementation

When unlockInternal() finds no waiter, it does:
  (2) d->waiters.fetchAndAddRelease(-BigNumber)
  (3) d_ptr.testAndSetRelease(d, nullptr)
  (4) d->derefWaiters(0): waiters.testAndSetRelaxed(-BigNumber, 0)
while a concurrent lockInternal(), holding a reference on d, does:
  (1) old_waiters = d->waiters.loadAcquire()
  (5) d->waiters.testAndSetRelaxed(old_waiters, old_waiters + 1)
  (6) if (d != d_ptr.loadAcquire()) retry; else d->wait()

If the locking thread reads at (1) or (5) the 0 written by (4), it must
see the d_ptr reset of (3) at (6). Otherwise it waits on a QMutexPrivate
that has already been detached from the mutex, and that no unlock will
ever signal: the mutex is unlocked (d_ptr == nullptr) but the thread
sleeps forever, with d->waiters == 1.

- (1) reads (4): QTBUG-88247 (d08e3b6de16118becaada17a58aed4042f400a5a)
  made (1) an acquire, but (4) is relaxed, so it does not synchronize
  with it: (4) is in the release sequence headed by (2), which comes
  before (3).
- (5) reads (4) (ABA): (1) read the 0 from before (2), then (2), (3) and
  (4) ran, and the relaxed CAS (5) succeeds against the 0 written by
  (4) without synchronizing with it.

Make (4) a release and (5) an acquire, so that (3) happens before (6) in
both cases. On x86 both CASes are already full barriers, so this changes
no code there. On AArch64 the bad outcome is allowed by the
architecture's memory model with the relaxed operations and forbidden
with this change (herd7 litmus tests in the bug report; the compiled
acquire loads are LDAPR, with the same results). It was seen as
a hang in Natron on Apple Silicon with Qt 5.15.19.

The non-futex path is used where QT_ALWAYS_USE_FUTEX is not defined:
QNX, VxWorks, INTEGRITY, OpenBSD, NetBSD, Hurd, Solaris, LSB builds,
wasm, and on Apple platforms up to 6.11 (6.0-6.6, and App Store
compliant builds of 6.7-6.11).

Fixes: QTBUG-NNNNNN
Task-number: QTBUG-88247
Pick-to: 6.12 6.11 6.8
---
--- a/src/corelib/thread/qmutex.cpp
+++ b/src/corelib/thread/qmutex.cpp
@@ -759,7 +759,9 @@
                     break;
                 }
             }
-        } while (!d->waiters.testAndSetRelaxed(old_waiters, old_waiters + 1));
+            // Acquire: if this reads the 0 that derefWaiters() stored in unlockInternal(), the
+            // d_ptr check below must see that unlockInternal() reset d_ptr before that.
+        } while (!d->waiters.testAndSetAcquire(old_waiters, old_waiters + 1));
 
         if (d != d_ptr.loadAcquire()) {
             // The mutex was unlocked before we incremented waiters.
@@ -942,7 +944,9 @@
             new_waiters += QMutexPrivate::BigNumber;
         }
         new_waiters -= value;
-    } while (!waiters.testAndSetRelaxed(old_waiters, new_waiters));
+        // Release: a thread in lockInternal() that reads this value must also see the d_ptr
+        // reset that unlockInternal() did before calling us.
+    } while (!waiters.testAndSetRelease(old_waiters, new_waiters));
 }
 #endif
 
